      {
        "id": "u2-t2",
        "title": "Queria: the polite way to order",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "rule",
            "title": "Quero or queria?",
            "text": "Querer means to want. Quero (I want) is direct. In cafés and shops people say queria (I'd like): softer and more polite."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "querer, present",
            "head": [
              "Person",
              "querer"
            ],
            "rows": [
